{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "mcp-doctor",
          "version": "1.0.0",
          "semanticVersion": "1.0.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "protocol/version-missing",
              "name": "protocol/version-missing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "initialize result has no protocolVersion"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Clients negotiate behaviour from the version the server reports. Without it the client cannot know which features are safe to use and may fall back to an incompatible code path."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/version-missing.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "initialize result has no protocolVersion. Clients negotiate behaviour from the version the server reports. Without it the client cannot know which features are safe to use and may fall back to an incompatible code path.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/version-missing.md",
                "markdown": "### initialize result has no protocolVersion\n\nClients negotiate behaviour from the version the server reports. Without it the client cannot know which features are safe to use and may fall back to an incompatible code path.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/version-missing.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "protocol",
                "tags": [
                  "protocol"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "spec": "lifecycle/initialization"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "protocol/version-unsupported",
              "name": "protocol/version-unsupported",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "server reports a protocol version mcp-doctor does not know"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An unknown version string usually means the server hard-coded a version instead of echoing the client's, or it is newer than the client and the negotiation silently failed."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/version-unsupported.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "server reports a protocol version mcp-doctor does not know. An unknown version string usually means the server hard-coded a version instead of echoing the client's, or it is newer than the client and the negotiation silently failed.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/version-unsupported.md",
                "markdown": "### server reports a protocol version mcp-doctor does not know\n\nAn unknown version string usually means the server hard-coded a version instead of echoing the client's, or it is newer than the client and the negotiation silently failed.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/version-unsupported.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "protocol",
                "tags": [
                  "protocol"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "spec": "lifecycle/initialization"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "protocol/stdout-pollution",
              "name": "protocol/stdout-pollution",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "non JSON-RPC output written to stdout"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "stdout is the message channel. A log line, banner or progress dot on stdout corrupts the stream and, depending on the client, either breaks parsing or silently drops the message that followed."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/stdout-pollution.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "non JSON-RPC output written to stdout. stdout is the message channel. A log line, banner or progress dot on stdout corrupts the stream and, depending on the client, either breaks parsing or silently drops the message that followed.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/stdout-pollution.md",
                "markdown": "### non JSON-RPC output written to stdout\n\nstdout is the message channel. A log line, banner or progress dot on stdout corrupts the stream and, depending on the client, either breaks parsing or silently drops the message that followed.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/stdout-pollution.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "protocol",
                "tags": [
                  "protocol"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "spec": "transports/stdio"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "protocol/list-failed",
              "name": "protocol/list-failed",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "a list method declared by capabilities failed"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Declaring a capability and then failing the matching list call leaves the client with a half-loaded server, usually with no explanation beyond a generic error."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/list-failed.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "a list method declared by capabilities failed. Declaring a capability and then failing the matching list call leaves the client with a half-loaded server, usually with no explanation beyond a generic error.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/list-failed.md",
                "markdown": "### a list method declared by capabilities failed\n\nDeclaring a capability and then failing the matching list call leaves the client with a half-loaded server, usually with no explanation beyond a generic error.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/list-failed.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "protocol",
                "tags": [
                  "protocol"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "protocol/no-capabilities",
              "name": "protocol/no-capabilities",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "server declares none of tools, resources or prompts"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A server with no capabilities exposes nothing to the model. This is almost always a wiring bug — a handler registered on the wrong object, or an early return before registration."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/no-capabilities.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "server declares none of tools, resources or prompts. A server with no capabilities exposes nothing to the model. This is almost always a wiring bug — a handler registered on the wrong object, or an early return before registration.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/no-capabilities.md",
                "markdown": "### server declares none of tools, resources or prompts\n\nA server with no capabilities exposes nothing to the model. This is almost always a wiring bug — a handler registered on the wrong object, or an early return before registration.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/no-capabilities.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "protocol",
                "tags": [
                  "protocol"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "spec": "lifecycle/initialization"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "protocol/server-info-incomplete",
              "name": "protocol/server-info-incomplete",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "serverInfo is missing name or version"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Clients show this to users and write it to logs. Without it, an incident report cannot tell which server produced a bad tool call."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/server-info-incomplete.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "serverInfo is missing name or version. Clients show this to users and write it to logs. Without it, an incident report cannot tell which server produced a bad tool call.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/server-info-incomplete.md",
                "markdown": "### serverInfo is missing name or version\n\nClients show this to users and write it to logs. Without it, an incident report cannot tell which server produced a bad tool call.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/server-info-incomplete.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "protocol",
                "tags": [
                  "protocol"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "warning",
                "spec": "lifecycle/initialization"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "protocol/instructions-missing",
              "name": "protocol/instructions-missing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "no initialize instructions provided"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "instructions is the one place a server can explain itself to the model without spending a tool description on it. Omitting it is allowed but the model then guesses how the tools fit together."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/instructions-missing.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "no initialize instructions provided. instructions is the one place a server can explain itself to the model without spending a tool description on it. Omitting it is allowed but the model then guesses how the tools fit together.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/instructions-missing.md",
                "markdown": "### no initialize instructions provided\n\ninstructions is the one place a server can explain itself to the model without spending a tool description on it. Omitting it is allowed but the model then guesses how the tools fit together.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/protocol/instructions-missing.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "protocol",
                "tags": [
                  "protocol"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "recommendation",
                "spec": "lifecycle/initialization"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "tools/name-missing",
              "name": "tools/name-missing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "tool has no name"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The name is the identifier the model calls. A tool without one is unreachable and is usually a serialization bug in the server's list handler."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/name-missing.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "tool has no name. The name is the identifier the model calls. A tool without one is unreachable and is usually a serialization bug in the server's list handler.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/name-missing.md",
                "markdown": "### tool has no name\n\nThe name is the identifier the model calls. A tool without one is unreachable and is usually a serialization bug in the server's list handler.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/name-missing.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "tools",
                "tags": [
                  "tools"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "spec": "server/tools"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "tools/name-format",
              "name": "tools/name-format",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "tool name uses characters outside [a-zA-Z0-9_-] or exceeds 64 chars"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Several clients and model APIs reject or transliterate names with dots, spaces, slashes or non-ASCII characters, which turns a working server into one that fails only on some hosts."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/name-format.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "tool name uses characters outside [a-zA-Z0-9_-] or exceeds 64 chars. Several clients and model APIs reject or transliterate names with dots, spaces, slashes or non-ASCII characters, which turns a working server into one that fails only on some hosts.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/name-format.md",
                "markdown": "### tool name uses characters outside [a-zA-Z0-9_-] or exceeds 64 chars\n\nSeveral clients and model APIs reject or transliterate names with dots, spaces, slashes or non-ASCII characters, which turns a working server into one that fails only on some hosts.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/name-format.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "tools",
                "tags": [
                  "tools"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "warning",
                "spec": "server/tools"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "tools/duplicate-name",
              "name": "tools/duplicate-name",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "two tools share the same name"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "With duplicate names the model's call is ambiguous and the client resolves it arbitrarily, so one of the two tools can never be invoked."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/duplicate-name.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "two tools share the same name. With duplicate names the model's call is ambiguous and the client resolves it arbitrarily, so one of the two tools can never be invoked.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/duplicate-name.md",
                "markdown": "### two tools share the same name\n\nWith duplicate names the model's call is ambiguous and the client resolves it arbitrarily, so one of the two tools can never be invoked.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/duplicate-name.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "tools",
                "tags": [
                  "tools"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "spec": "server/tools"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "tools/description-missing",
              "name": "tools/description-missing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "tool has no description"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The description is the only thing the model sees when choosing between tools. Without it the model either never calls the tool or calls it with guessed arguments."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/description-missing.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "tool has no description. The description is the only thing the model sees when choosing between tools. Without it the model either never calls the tool or calls it with guessed arguments.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/description-missing.md",
                "markdown": "### tool has no description\n\nThe description is the only thing the model sees when choosing between tools. Without it the model either never calls the tool or calls it with guessed arguments.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/description-missing.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "tools",
                "tags": [
                  "tools"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "spec": "server/tools"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "tools/description-too-short",
              "name": "tools/description-too-short",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "description shorter than 20 characters"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A two-word description such as \"gets data\" gives the model no basis to prefer this tool over a similar one, which shows up as erratic tool selection rather than an obvious bug."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/description-too-short.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "description shorter than 20 characters. A two-word description such as \"gets data\" gives the model no basis to prefer this tool over a similar one, which shows up as erratic tool selection rather than an obvious bug.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/description-too-short.md",
                "markdown": "### description shorter than 20 characters\n\nA two-word description such as \"gets data\" gives the model no basis to prefer this tool over a similar one, which shows up as erratic tool selection rather than an obvious bug.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/description-too-short.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "tools",
                "tags": [
                  "tools"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "warning",
                "spec": "server/tools"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "tools/description-too-long",
              "name": "tools/description-too-long",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "description longer than 1024 characters"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Every description is resent on every turn. One verbose tool can dominate the context window and crowd out the conversation it was meant to help with."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/description-too-long.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "description longer than 1024 characters. Every description is resent on every turn. One verbose tool can dominate the context window and crowd out the conversation it was meant to help with.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/description-too-long.md",
                "markdown": "### description longer than 1024 characters\n\nEvery description is resent on every turn. One verbose tool can dominate the context window and crowd out the conversation it was meant to help with.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/description-too-long.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "tools",
                "tags": [
                  "tools"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "warning",
                "spec": "server/tools"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "tools/input-schema-missing",
              "name": "tools/input-schema-missing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "tool has no inputSchema"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "inputSchema is required by the specification. Without it a strict client rejects the tool outright and a lenient one lets the model invent arguments."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/input-schema-missing.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "tool has no inputSchema. inputSchema is required by the specification. Without it a strict client rejects the tool outright and a lenient one lets the model invent arguments.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/input-schema-missing.md",
                "markdown": "### tool has no inputSchema\n\ninputSchema is required by the specification. Without it a strict client rejects the tool outright and a lenient one lets the model invent arguments.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/input-schema-missing.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "tools",
                "tags": [
                  "tools"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "spec": "server/tools"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "tools/input-schema-not-object",
              "name": "tools/input-schema-not-object",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "inputSchema does not describe an object"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Tool arguments are always a JSON object. A schema typed as string or array makes the model emit a shape the server cannot parse."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/input-schema-not-object.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "inputSchema does not describe an object. Tool arguments are always a JSON object. A schema typed as string or array makes the model emit a shape the server cannot parse.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/input-schema-not-object.md",
                "markdown": "### inputSchema does not describe an object\n\nTool arguments are always a JSON object. A schema typed as string or array makes the model emit a shape the server cannot parse.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/input-schema-not-object.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "tools",
                "tags": [
                  "tools"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "error",
                "spec": "server/tools"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "tools/parameter-description-missing",
              "name": "tools/parameter-description-missing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "a declared parameter has no description"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Parameter names alone rarely disambiguate: is `id` a numeric row id, a UUID or a slug? Models fill that gap by guessing, and the guess is invisible until the call fails."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/parameter-description-missing.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "a declared parameter has no description. Parameter names alone rarely disambiguate: is `id` a numeric row id, a UUID or a slug? Models fill that gap by guessing, and the guess is invisible until the call fails.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/parameter-description-missing.md",
                "markdown": "### a declared parameter has no description\n\nParameter names alone rarely disambiguate: is `id` a numeric row id, a UUID or a slug? Models fill that gap by guessing, and the guess is invisible until the call fails.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/parameter-description-missing.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "tools",
                "tags": [
                  "tools"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "warning",
                "spec": "server/tools"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "tools/schema-fragile-keywords",
              "name": "tools/schema-fragile-keywords",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "inputSchema uses keywords many tool-call clients handle poorly"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Composition keywords such as $ref, oneOf and allOf are valid JSON Schema but are frequently flattened or ignored by client-side validators, so the model sees a looser contract than the one you wrote."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/schema-fragile-keywords.md",
              "help": {
                "text": "inputSchema uses keywords many tool-call clients handle poorly. Composition keywords such as $ref, oneOf and allOf are valid JSON Schema but are frequently flattened or ignored by client-side validators, so the model sees a looser contract than the one you wrote.\n\nDocumentation: https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/schema-fragile-keywords.md",
                "markdown": "### inputSchema uses keywords many tool-call clients handle poorly\n\nComposition keywords such as $ref, oneOf and allOf are valid JSON Schema but are frequently flattened or ignored by client-side validators, so the model sees a looser contract than the one you wrote.\n\n**Documentation**: [Rule Documentation](https://github.com/bakhtiyor-aminzoda/mcp-linter/blob/main/docs/rules/tools/schema-fragile-keywords.md)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "category": "tools",
                "tags": [
                  "tools"
                ],
                "precision": "very-high",
                "problem.severity": "recommendation",
                "spec": "server/tools"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "tools/annotations-missing",
              "name": "tools/annotations-missing",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "tool has no annotations at all"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "annotations is how a server describes the blast radius of a call — read-only, destructive, idempotent, open-world. Clients use it for confirmation prompts, and hosts use it for policy."
              },
